      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This behavior gets far more visible when laying down. On every avatar I tested, the head sinks into and through the shoulders when laying down with full body.\nEDIT: Investigated a bit more. First of all, this seems to be linked to https://vrchat.canny.io/avatar-30/p/bug-fullbody-broke-on-my-previously-compatible-avatar\nSee my images below, but I think most of this is related to the IK now weighting the head higher than before, in previous builds the head would sink or rise a little bit when the avatar wasn't completely straight. Now when tilting the head the upper chest moves in opposition to the head to give more room.\nWhen laying down, I'm not sure what's happening since the eyes are even farther below my viewpoint. In the second image I'm pointing at the center of my viewpoint, where in the first, it's lined up.\nBoth of these happen consistently in every vaguely human shaped avatar I've tried.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
